they have the 2nd most pass rushers in the league.","special":"The Bears have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 73% of field goals, which is well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 8% of the money on the books.","players":"Caleb Williams has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,020 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Luther Burden III and Colston Loveland leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. D'Andre Swift has handled most of the work in the backfield with 55% of the carries. On defense, Austin Booker leads the team with 4 sacks.","coaching":"Ben Johnson is calling the offense as head coach and Dennis Allen is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Vikings under Kevin O'Connell and the 2023 Lions under Ben Johnson. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Buccaneers under Todd Bowles and the 2023 Cowboys under Dan Quinn.","trends":"The offense went from 8th in EPA per play in 2025 to 12th so far this season, a modest decline. The defense moved from 19th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 16th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 12% to 0%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}